## Acceptance

In order to get any license under these terms, you must agree
to them as both strict obligations and conditions of all
your licenses.

## Copyright License

The licensor grants you a copyright license for the software
to do everything you might do with the software that is
not prohibited by these terms, except for the right to
license the software.

## Noncompete

In addition to the restrictions in the copyright license,
you may not use the software, or the value derived from
the software, to make a product, service, or other thing
that earns revenue, or to aid anyone else in doing so.

## Patent License

The licensor grants you a patent license for the software
that covers patent claims the licensor can license, or
becomes able to license, that you would infringe by using
the software.

## Noncompete Patent License

In addition to the restrictions in the patent license, you
may not use the software, or the value derived from
the software, to make a product, service, or other thing
that earns revenue, or to aid anyone else in doing so.

## Notices

You must ensure that anyone who gets a copy of any part of
the software from you also gets a copy of these terms,
all the copyright, patent, and trademark notices in the
software, and this notice.

## No Other Rights

These terms do not allow you to sublicense or transfer any
of your licenses to anyone else, or prevent the licensor
from granting licenses to anyone else. These terms do not
imply any other licenses.

## Patent Defense

If you make any written claim that the software infringes
or contributes to infringement of any patent, your patent
license for the software granted under these terms ends
immediately. If your company makes such a claim, your
patent license ends immediately for work on behalf of
your company.

## Violations

The first time you are notified in writing of any violation
of these terms, your licenses are reinstated retroactively
unless you secured relief in writing from the party that
notified you before the 32nd day after the notification.
If you violate these terms again after that, all your
licenses end immediately.

## No Liability

***As far as the law allows, the software comes as is,
without any warranty or condition, and the licensor will
not be liable to you for any damages arising out of these
terms or the software, under any kind of legal claim.***

## Definitions

The "licensor" is the individual or entity offering these
terms, and the "software" is the software the licensor
makes available under these terms.

"You" refers to the individual or entity agreeing to these
terms.

"Use" means anything you do with the software requiring
one of the licensor's permissions.

"Revenue" means payment, or other value received, for
your or a related party's benefit, for or in connection
with the software.

"Related party" means anyone who controls, is controlled
by, or is under common control with you.
